<article class="home">
    <header class="hero">
        <h1>Watch a router think</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
            Every click in this lab runs through ModRouter. The strip above shows what it sees: the address, the route levels that
            matched, and each stage the navigation passed through. Fire a few navigations and watch the signal travel.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <button class="btn" @onclick="@(() => Navigation.NavigateToRoute("ship", new { id = 2 }))">Open a ship</button>
            <button class="btn btn-quiet" @onclick="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/nowhere/at/all"))">Ask for a page that does not exist</button>
            <RouteLink Route="l1" Match="RouteLinkMatch.Exact" Class="btn btn-quiet">Start lesson 1</RouteLink>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="home-grid" aria-label="The lessons">
        @foreach (var lesson in LessonCatalog.All)
        {
            <RouteLink Route="@lesson.RouteName" Match="RouteLinkMatch.Exact" Class="lesson-card">
                <span class="dot">@lesson.Number</span>
                <b>@lesson.Title</b>
                <span>@lesson.Promise</span>
            </RouteLink>
        }
    </section>

    <p class="home-foot">
        Each lesson is a real ModRouter feature with its code in this repository. The written walkthrough that goes with them is in the
        <a href="https://modrouter.github.io/blazor-modrouter/ModRouter/docs/lessons.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">guided lessons</a>.
    </p>
</article>
